# Tasks - Scenario 3

## Backend - Drawing & Guessing Logic
- [x] Add `canvasData`, `guesses`, and `scores` to `Room` and `RoomSnapshot` in `backend/src/models/game.ts`.
- [x] Define `Guess` interface.
- [x] Implement `updateCanvas(code: string, participantId: string, data: string)` in `backend/src/services/roomStore.ts`.
- [x] Implement `submitGuess(code: string, participantId: string, text: string)` in `backend/src/services/roomStore.ts`.
  - [x] Validate guesser is NOT the drawer.
  - [x] Compare guess case-insensitively with `secretWord`.
  - [x] Update `guesses` history.
  - [x] Update `scores` if correct (+100).
- [x] Add `POST /rooms/:code/draw` and `POST /rooms/:code/guess` in `backend/src/api/rooms.ts`.

## Frontend - Interactive Gameplay UI
- [x] Update `api` service with `draw` and `submitGuess` methods in `frontend/src/services/api.ts`.
- [x] Implement `draw` and `submitGuess` in `frontend/src/state/roomStore.ts`.
- [x] In `GamePage.tsx`, update "Canvas" card to show actual `canvasData` status.
- [x] In `GamePage.tsx`, hook up "Clear Canvas" to `roomStore.draw("")`.
- [x] In `GamePage.tsx`, simulate drawing by clicking on the canvas area (calls `roomStore.draw("drawn")`).
- [x] Update `Scoreboard.tsx` to display scores from `room.scores`.
- [x] Update `GuessForm.tsx` to call `roomStore.submitGuess(text)`.
- [x] Display guess history in `GamePage.tsx` or a separate panel.

## Validation
- [x] Verify drawer can "draw" and clear the canvas.
- [x] Verify guessers see updated canvas status via polling.
- [x] Verify guessers can submit guesses.
- [x] Verify correct guesses increase score by 100.
- [x] Verify guess history is visible to all players.
- [x] Verify drawer cannot submit guesses.
